' Source companion for the built-in `process` package (plan-90).
'
' The opaque `Process` resource handle is native-declared in the `.rs` front end
' (`src/builtins/process.rs`); this file carries only the value enums the package
' exposes: `Stream` (plan-90-B, which child stream a read reads from) and `Signal`
' (plan-90-C). Every callable stays native — there are zero source-EXPORT public
' functions here (the established built-in-package idiom).

DOC
  ENUM Stream
  DESC Selects which of a spawned child's output streams a `process::receive`,
  DESC `process::receiveBytes`, or `process::poll` reads from. The default
  DESC overload (no `from` argument) reads standard output.
  PROP StdOut The child's standard output.
  PROP StdErr The child's standard error.
END DOC
EXPORT ENUM Stream
  StdOut          ' the child's standard output (the default)
  StdErr          ' the child's standard error
END ENUM

DOC
  ENUM Signal
  DESC A cross-platform signal bucket. `process::signal` delivers one to a child
  DESC (`Kill`→SIGKILL, `Terminate`→SIGTERM, `Error`→SIGABRT, `None`→no-op);
  DESC `process::didSignal` reports which bucket a terminated child died on
  DESC (`None` if it exited normally or has not terminated).
  PROP None No signal (a no-op to send; "exited normally / still running" to read).
  PROP Kill Forced, uncatchable termination (SIGKILL).
  PROP Terminate A polite "please stop" (SIGTERM and the other catchable stops).
  PROP Error An abnormal-fault termination (SIGABRT/SIGSEGV/SIGFPE/…).
END DOC
EXPORT ENUM Signal
  None            ' no signal (send: no-op; observe: normal exit / still running)
  Kill            ' SIGKILL
  Terminate       ' SIGTERM (and other catchable stop signals)
  Error           ' SIGABRT/SIGSEGV/SIGFPE/… (abnormal fault)
END ENUM
